      "created_at": "2018-07-25T12:50:18Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-07-25T12:50:34Z",
      "body": "@ajoecker GDPR is not applicable for anonymized data.\r\nConsent is only required when collecting personally identifiable information.\r\n\r\nRecital 26 of the Data Protection Directive (95/46/EC) provides that:\r\n \r\n“…to determine whether a person is identifiable, account should be taken of all the means likely reasonably to be used either by the controller or by any other person to identify the said person… the principles of [data] protection shall not apply to data .rendered anonymous in such a way that the data subject is no longer identifiable…”",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "pin": null,
